        "hub_id":  null,
        "version":  "4.7.0",
        "description":  "\u003cp\u003eAdded an option to backport the Kordbreach / EFT 1.1.0.0 Collector prerequisites based on \u003ca target=\"_blank\" class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://x.com/tarkov/status/2077755562490581359\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e@tarkov’s recent tweet\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdded a new setting \u003ccode\u003equestOverrides\u003c/code\u003e that allows overriding the settings from \u003ccode\u003eremoveConditions\u003c/code\u003e for individual quests.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRepeating the example in the description, Forester’s Duty could be expanded from villages to the entire maps to match live by adding \u003ccode\u003e{\"66ab9da7eb102b9bcd08591c\": {\"zone\": true}}\u003c/code\u003e while leaving the zones for other quests like Capturing Outposts and Secured Perimeter in effect.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen using the \u003ccode\u003eonlyQuests\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eexemptQuests\u003c/code\u003e settings, overrides will \u003cem\u003ealways\u003c/em\u003e take effect but will only fall back to the global/default settings in \u003ccode\u003eremoveConditions\u003c/code\u003e depending on the quest’s presence in those settings.\u003c/p\u003e\n",
